WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 31 Student Video
Unit 8, Lesson 3: Doubt

1
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.940
Since I grew up in a Christian home, the Christian story always made sense to me.

2
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.700
My parents have worked their entire lives with a professional Christian ministry.

3
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:24.800
My dad has spent his life writing, speaking, and debating the truth of the

4
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.100
Christian message. Yet when I was in my upper teens, I had some questions that kind

5
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.180
of troubled me that seemed more pertinent in my life than ever before.

6
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.700
Questions like, how do I really know that Christianity is true?

7
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.520
What if I was born in a different family or in a different culture, would I still

8
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.740
believe the Christian message? What if my beliefs are false?

9
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.080
I decided it was time to share my doubts and my questions with my father, not

10
00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:58.840
knowing how he would respond. After all, he spent his life teaching the

11
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.400
Christian message to others. We were up in the mountains at a small coffee shop and

12
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.480
I remember leaning into my dad and saying, Dad, I want to know what's true.

13
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.140
but I don't know that I'm convinced that Christianity is true and he instantly

14
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.260
looked right back at me he goes son I think that's great and for a second I said

15
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.080
wait a minute dad did you hear what I just said I'm doubting Christianity and he

16
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.920
said I did hear you, son and I think this is good because you can't live your life

17
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:31.540
based on my convictions you have to come to a point where you know and believe

18
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:36.980
that christianity is true for yourself he said don't rebel just for the sake of

19
00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:41.100
rebelling so many young people growing up reject what their parents taught them just

20
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.900
out of spite he said if you walk away only do so because you're convinced that

21
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:51.340
christianity is not true and no matter what you decide you need to know that your

22
00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.300
mom and i will always love you doubts and questions are not bad whenever

23
00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.900
my students come up to me and say hey Mr.

24
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.480
McDowell I've got some questions and doubts I always respond by saying that's

25
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.400
fantastic I'm so glad you're asking these questions now that's not the typical

26
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.500
response that they expect because sometimes we think that asking questions and

27
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:19.240
doubting God and His Word can be bad but that's not always the case you see

28
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:24.460
doubts can be good if we see them as opportunities to go deeper in our faith

29
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:29.360
it's not doubts that are bad it's unexpressed doubts that can be bad.

30
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.640
You see, it's not doubts that are corrosive to faith.

31
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.880
It's when we have doubts and we don't seek answers.

32
00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:41.240
So if you have doubts about your faith, the first thing to do is to just share them

33
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.640
with somebody and start the conversation.

34
00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.140
There are a variety of reasons that might motivate someone to have questions and

35
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:55.080
doubts. some can certainly be intellectual but I'm convinced that more

36
00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.920
often than not the source of a doubt the heart of a doubt comes from emotional

37
00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:06.880
relational or moral reasons consider a couple stories that might help

38
00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:12.500
first I met a young man while speaking at a conference in Chicago and when I was

39
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.000
done he came up to me said hey can we go outside and talk a little further i've got

40
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.100
some questions for you some doubts about my faith i said sure so he went outside and

41
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.960
he had some questions about whether jesus could really be god he had questions about

42
00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.060
other religions and after doing my best to answer his questions i sensed that

43
00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.660
something deeper was going on i said something to the effect of you know i'm

44
00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.820
answering your questions but i think something else is going on with you what is it

45
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:41.460
and essentially came out he admitted he said you know what i was raised in the

46
00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.340
christian faith but i'm just about to graduate from high school, I'm heading

47
00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.360
to college and I've joined a fraternity.

48
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.400
I just want to have some fun. And then it hit me.

49
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.580
Although he raised intellectual questions and challenges to the faith, that wasn't

50
00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.020
the heart of his doubt. The heart of his doubts were moral.

51
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.840
He wanted to live a certain way and saw his Christian beliefs as getting in the way

52
00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.060
of what he thought would be the most fun.

53
00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:15.620
Second, our relationships can deeply affect the way we relate to God.

54
00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:21.580
Take my father for example he had a distant and a drunk father so he would hear

55
00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.980
people say things like hey you have a heavenly father who loves you my dad but think

56
00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:31.560
wait a minute father equals hurt and distance and pain why would I want a

57
00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.580
Heavenly Father when it just brings more pain?

58
00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.660
You see the reality is our relationships, especially our broken relationships,

59
00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.960
can drive questions and doubts about God.

60
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.260
An important question we really need to ask ourselves is, how have our

61
00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:51.560
relationships, the ones that have been good and the ones that have failed, affected

62
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.340
the way we view and relate to God?

63
00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.340
For many people, the experience...

64
00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.280
Hang on, I gotta deal with this.

65
00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.990
People who go through doubts will often describe it as if the ground is crumbling

66
00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:16.050
beneath them, or they're fumbling around in the dark.

67
00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.570
The experience of doubts can be very painful and can bring up a lot of fears.

68
00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.430
That's why one of the place to begin with is to really identify what's at the heart,

69
00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.610
what's at the source of my doubts.

70
00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:33.350
And this requires a lot of searching.

71
00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:41.280
Surprisingly, one of the most prominent examples of doubt in the Bible comes from

72
00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:46.140
John the Baptist, the prophesied forerunner of Christ the Messiah.

73
00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:51.520
Herod had John the Baptist arrested, thrown in prison and he sends his disciples to

74
00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:56.080
Jesus to ask him, are you the one or should we expect another?

75
00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:01.640
Well the question is why did John the Baptist have questions and doubts at this

76
00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:05.960
point in his life? And the answer is because he was alone and he was suffering.

77
00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.560
Loneliness and pain are common reasons why people have questions and doubts about

78
00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:12.940
God.

79
00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.140
Jesus's response is powerful. He doesn't scold John.

80
00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:23.380
He doesn't chastise him. He doesn't show disappointment in John for having questions

81
00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:27.460
and doubts. Rather, he gives John evidence.

82
00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:33.380
In Luke 7:22 through 23, it describes how Jesus says to his

83
00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:37.800
disciples, go back and tell John what you have seen and what you have heard.

84
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:43.840
The deaf hear, the blind see, the lame walk, and the dead

85
00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.140
live again, and the poor have the good news preached to them.

86
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:11.460
So what does this tell us? Well, for one thing, it tells that doubts are a normal

87
00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:17.040
and natural part of life. All of us should expect to have questions at some

88
00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:22.340
point in our journey of faith. In fact, even the apostles had doubts.

89
00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:27.980
It says in Matthew 28 that they worshiped Jesus as God and yet some of them

90
00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:33.620
doubted. Can you imagine that? The very people who saw the risen

91
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:39.580
Jesus had doubts. If John the Baptist and the apostles had doubts,

92
00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:44.940
you better believe that some of us, if not most of us, will have doubts at some

93
00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:50.840
point in our life. That's why I believe that Jude 22 says to have mercy on those who

94
00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:51.080
doubt.

95
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.600
Doubt is not the opposite of faith.

96
00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:07.200
In fact, doubt can often serve as the basis for developing a more robust

97
00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:12.280
faith. The key is to identify what is the source of the doubt.

98
00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:17.300
If your doubts are emotional you might need to find and experience some emotional

99
00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:22.660
healing. If your doubts are relational, you might need to restore some broken

100
00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:27.860
relationships. And if your doubts are intellectual, you need to find some answers to

101
00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:33.640
your questions. You see, doubt is not necessarily corrosive to faith, but can be the

102
00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:37.940
opportunity to develop a deeper and a lasting faith.

